WEBVTT

00:08.150 --> 00:14.860
<i>Mash was chosen as a player for Duelo,
an aerial magic sport using brooms.</i>

00:23.500 --> 00:27.500
<i>However, he can't use magic,
so he couldn't fly.</i>

00:28.500 --> 00:29.800
I want to go home.

00:30.210 --> 00:31.510
<i>Yeah, you should.</i>

02:02.560 --> 02:05.060
What are you doing? Get flying already!

02:05.060 --> 02:06.480
Is this match rigged?

02:07.060 --> 02:09.350
Mash, you need to start flying soon.

02:09.350 --> 02:11.310
What's wrong, Mash?

02:12.520 --> 02:14.020
Hey, Mash.

02:14.280 --> 02:15.940
Oh, Captain.

02:16.650 --> 02:20.240
Are you glistening in the fire called life?
Is your heart throbbing?

02:21.450 --> 02:22.620
I don't get it.

02:22.830 --> 02:25.160
You swore that we would be number one!

02:25.160 --> 02:26.700
I didn't.

02:26.700 --> 02:28.500
Don't be complacent!

02:28.500 --> 02:30.170
I'm not.

02:30.170 --> 02:32.420
Mash! Remember the mighty bamboo!

02:32.420 --> 02:33.130
Bamboo?

02:33.290 --> 02:38.170
Bamboo can survive any climate!
They're strong and supple!

02:38.170 --> 02:41.800
That's what you're lacking right now!
And it’s bamboo!

02:41.800 --> 02:45.640
- Bamboo, bamboo, bamboo. Bamboo it!
- This guy has to be high.

02:46.470 --> 02:50.230
Oh, right. I haven't told you
the rules for Duelo yet.

02:50.230 --> 02:51.770
It's pretty simple.

02:51.770 --> 02:56.070
We fight over control of the ball midair.
Pass it through that ring for a point.

02:57.400 --> 02:59.150
Wait, they scored another point?

03:00.860 --> 03:02.910
Magic is forbidden.

03:02.910 --> 03:05.280
This sport is all about your broom technique.

03:05.990 --> 03:08.660
Bamboo that can't fly are just shoots!

03:08.660 --> 03:11.540
<i>He doesn't think at all
before he speaks.</i>

03:13.330 --> 03:17.710
This goes without saying,
but I put everything into Duelo.

03:19.130 --> 03:20.840
That's why I recruited you.

03:24.010 --> 03:25.680
I'm heading back out there.

03:26.310 --> 03:27.680
It's all up to you now.

03:37.150 --> 03:40.440
Lord Tom, last year's
Duelo MVP of the year is...

03:40.440 --> 03:44.200
Lord Tom, the sportsman whose
stuffiness actually works well is...

03:44.450 --> 03:47.950
Oops, sorry. That was an accident.

03:49.870 --> 03:51.000
Captain...

03:53.420 --> 03:55.330
An additional point for Lang dorm!

03:55.330 --> 03:58.210
They have a 40 point lead
against Adler dorm!

03:59.000 --> 04:00.340
Are you okay?

04:00.340 --> 04:03.880
Sorry. I think I broke a bone.

04:04.680 --> 04:07.470
Wh-Where's your sense of sportsmanship?

04:07.760 --> 04:08.640
Huh?

04:08.640 --> 04:11.730
Sportsmanship is nonsense.

04:11.980 --> 04:14.140
All that matters is winning.

04:15.150 --> 04:18.570
Keep huddling, wusses!

04:22.400 --> 04:23.900
How pathetic.

04:23.900 --> 04:25.660
There isn't much time left.

04:25.660 --> 04:27.780
And they've got a huge lead.

04:28.740 --> 04:31.870
But Mash, I just want you to know...

04:32.370 --> 04:34.500
Winning isn't what matters!

04:34.500 --> 04:36.500
What matters is
whether you gave it your all!

04:41.170 --> 04:43.670
Another point for Lang dorm!

04:43.670 --> 04:46.510
Will this lead be impossible to diminish?

04:46.800 --> 04:50.010
With two down, it's only natural we win.

04:53.390 --> 04:54.560
Mash...

05:01.860 --> 05:02.900
He flew!

05:02.900 --> 05:06.360
H-Hey! Look, he's stopped in midair!

05:06.360 --> 05:07.450
You're kidding me!

05:07.450 --> 05:08.950
He was able to fly?

05:13.450 --> 05:17.210
<i>He's sure kicking his legs a lot.</i>

05:17.880 --> 05:19.420
Time for a thrashing.

05:20.380 --> 05:21.880
Hey, pass it here!

05:22.210 --> 05:23.670
S-Sure.

05:25.970 --> 05:28.180
Hey, he's got the ball.

05:28.180 --> 05:30.390
What's he gonna do from that distance?

05:30.390 --> 05:31.970
Is he joking?

05:33.390 --> 05:36.560
He can't even ride a broom.
What makes him think...

05:38.560 --> 05:42.480
I'll take that from ya, you nobody!

05:54.040 --> 05:55.500
Adler dorm scores!

05:55.500 --> 05:57.250
What an amazing shot!

05:57.670 --> 06:01.290
They're still down 49 points,
and time's nearly up!

06:01.290 --> 06:04.000
Wait! Look at that! The ball!

06:07.380 --> 06:09.260
What!?

06:17.730 --> 06:22.020
What unnaturally strong fingers!
That curve-ball was out of this world!

06:46.960 --> 06:48.220
No way.

06:48.220 --> 06:49.550
What the...

06:49.720 --> 06:50.970
Freaky.

06:50.970 --> 06:53.010
But that score...

06:53.010 --> 06:55.310
It's undeniable.

06:55.560 --> 07:00.810
<i>The winner of the first Duelo match
for this season is Adler dorm!</i>

07:01.810 --> 07:04.020
Not bad for looking like a fungus!

07:04.020 --> 07:05.820
Sorry for telling you to go home!

07:05.820 --> 07:06.440
Totes sorry for throwing garbage at you!

07:06.440 --> 07:07.990
<i>Mash and the Adler dorm team
scored a record-high</i>
Totes sorry for throwing garbage at you!

07:07.990 --> 07:11.280
<i>Mash and the Adler dorm team
scored a record-high</i>

07:11.490 --> 07:15.200
<i>and were given silver coins.</i>

07:15.990 --> 07:18.000
What's with this shape?

07:18.250 --> 07:20.460
Wow, that was an amazing game!

07:20.460 --> 07:23.500
And you got a silver coin
so soon after transferring here.

07:23.500 --> 07:25.750
Thanks, but I’m never doing that again.

07:25.750 --> 07:27.000
Hey, Mash!

07:28.050 --> 07:29.720
It's Lord Tom!

07:29.970 --> 07:32.220
Huh? What? What's going on?

07:33.590 --> 07:34.640
Thank you!

07:34.640 --> 07:37.470
You turned into one great bamboo!

07:37.470 --> 07:41.020
You really grew there, bamboo!
You overshot me, bamboo! Did you feel it?
<i>I don't really get along with this type.
At all.</i>

07:41.020 --> 07:42.230
You really grew there, bamboo!
You overshot me, bamboo! Did you feel it?

07:43.770 --> 07:45.060
<i>First-year student Mash,</i>

07:45.060 --> 07:50.110
<i>the key player of the game
who broke the record for game score,</i>

07:50.110 --> 07:56.080
<i>said in his interview he credits his success
to his upperclassman's exuberant encouragement.</i>

07:56.080 --> 07:59.200
<i>Quite a humble answer
despite such a great record.</i>

08:00.830 --> 08:03.870
The one from the entrance exams.

08:06.130 --> 08:10.630
He risked failing for a complete stranger.

08:12.170 --> 08:13.590
What naivete.

08:17.350 --> 08:19.220
He'll be next.

08:23.270 --> 08:25.600
<i>And the next day.</i>

08:25.980 --> 08:28.650
Mash, it's time for Duelo practice!

08:28.650 --> 08:31.780
Shoot for the stars! Even if you miss,
you'll land among your dreams!

08:32.070 --> 08:37.030
Mash, I heard you have trouble studying,
so let's study together!

08:37.200 --> 08:39.450
You swore to me
that we'd take the top together!

08:39.450 --> 08:40.370
I didn't.

08:40.370 --> 08:45.080
I have Potions, Magic History,
Enchantment, Divination, and...

08:45.080 --> 08:46.080
Way too much.

08:46.080 --> 08:47.710
Don't be complacent!

08:47.710 --> 08:49.380
We are bamboo. Bamboo!

08:49.380 --> 08:54.550
And you have to properly study
Magical Creatures and Dark Arts as well.

08:54.800 --> 08:56.590
What's important is bamboo!
You'll land among your dreams with bamboo!

08:56.590 --> 08:58.050
Finn, help me.
What's important is bamboo!
You'll land among your dreams with bamboo!

08:58.050 --> 08:58.760
What's important is bamboo!
You'll land among your dreams with bamboo!

09:00.470 --> 09:01.970
Traitor.

09:02.180 --> 09:04.230
That head of yours is not
a mushroom, but a bamboo!

09:04.230 --> 09:06.150
You seem to be having fun.
That head of yours is not
a mushroom, but a bamboo!

09:08.230 --> 09:10.190
Mind if I join?

09:12.820 --> 09:13.940
<i>This guy...</i>

09:13.940 --> 09:16.910
<i>He has two marks.
I've never seen him before.</i>

09:17.110 --> 09:18.200
<i>Could he be a first year?</i>

09:18.410 --> 09:22.750
<i>That's Lance Crown.
He ranked first in the entrance exams.</i>

09:22.750 --> 09:25.790
<i>Seeing him up close, he's a total hottie.</i>

09:26.080 --> 09:29.920
<i>No, I can't!
I've given my heart to someone else.</i>

09:31.000 --> 09:33.050
No, it's not fun.

09:33.050 --> 09:37.180
I see. Then let's do something
that is fun.

09:37.720 --> 09:39.180
Something fun?

09:40.390 --> 09:41.680
Hide and seek?

09:41.680 --> 09:44.020
Definitely not hide and seek!

09:44.730 --> 09:47.770
This bottle is a special magical tool.

09:48.190 --> 09:50.520
It's quite ancient.

09:56.070 --> 09:58.030
But as you can see,
it's capable of trapping people.

09:58.030 --> 09:59.200
- What's this?
- What in the world?
But as you can see,
it's capable of trapping people.

09:59.200 --> 10:00.530
- What's this?
- What in the world?

10:00.530 --> 10:04.500
Stuck in a small space with two guys
has compliance issues!

10:04.950 --> 10:09.580
If you want it back,
come to the forest next to the owl hut.

10:09.580 --> 10:10.880
I'll be waiting.

10:23.100 --> 10:24.270
What's this about?

10:24.270 --> 10:25.520
Call it a bet.

10:25.720 --> 10:29.650
You're after them too, aren't you?
These coins?

10:29.900 --> 10:32.860
A silver coin?
And he's got two of them!

10:32.860 --> 10:35.650
I thought only a select number
of upperclassmen had them!

10:36.740 --> 10:42.240
And the lines on your mark reveal
the amount of magic power you currently have.

10:42.490 --> 10:45.410
This guy is really bad news!

10:48.960 --> 10:50.750
<i>Single-line magic users.</i>

10:51.210 --> 10:54.380
<i>A term used to specify those
with just one mark on their face.</i>

10:55.630 --> 10:59.880
<i>The majority of people in this world
are single-line magic users.</i>

11:00.930 --> 11:04.970
<i>But there are rare exceptions
with multiple marks.</i>

11:06.020 --> 11:07.810
<i>Double-line magic users.</i>

11:08.350 --> 11:12.440
<i>They exist in this realm
at a rate of one in 100,000.</i>

11:13.150 --> 11:15.900
<i>They're considered chosen
by magic itself.</i>

11:16.900 --> 11:20.200
We'll bet each other's silver coin in a match.

11:20.650 --> 11:23.490
We'll go until the loser
can no longer continue or gives up.

11:24.160 --> 11:28.620
Any other duel involving magic
is considered taboo in this school.

11:29.460 --> 11:32.710
Not that you have
any choice but to accept.

11:32.710 --> 11:34.960
Not as long as I hold this, that is.

11:37.210 --> 11:44.090
And judging by your personality, the fact that
I even possess this plays to my favor.

11:44.970 --> 11:48.970
Not that I need the handicap.
It's easy enough to tell who would win.

11:49.850 --> 11:53.150
During the entrance exams,
you were too soft.

11:53.810 --> 11:57.440
You prioritized someone else
over your own goals.

11:58.650 --> 12:03.240
I could never lose
against a slacker like that.

12:03.490 --> 12:03.780
Don't do it, Mash! He's dangerous!

12:03.780 --> 12:05.740
It's over. My life is going to end!
Don't do it, Mash! He's dangerous!

12:05.740 --> 12:08.740
That's right!
I've got a bad feeling about him!
It's over. My life is going to end!

12:09.700 --> 12:12.210
What's wrong? Too scared to respond?

12:12.830 --> 12:17.000
No. Enough of that.
Hurry up and get on with it.

12:18.380 --> 12:20.340
At least you've got spirit.

12:23.090 --> 12:26.930
But first, let's make things a bit easier.

12:28.100 --> 12:28.760
Graviole.

12:35.940 --> 12:39.320
I wonder if Mash is doing okay.

12:39.980 --> 12:40.940
I'm worried.

12:41.070 --> 12:41.740
What?

12:41.740 --> 12:45.030
No, I'm talking about my profits.

12:45.660 --> 12:47.410
I-I see.

12:51.450 --> 12:53.040
Wh-Wha...

12:53.330 --> 12:55.790
What the hell is this?

13:02.840 --> 13:04.930
This makes things easier.

13:06.470 --> 13:08.300
Flashy performances...

13:09.970 --> 13:11.060
are unnecessary!

13:11.270 --> 13:13.810
Trying to win against me without magic?

13:14.140 --> 13:15.060
Graviole.

13:18.360 --> 13:19.230
Mash!

13:20.150 --> 13:22.030
Are you being serious?

13:22.280 --> 13:24.610
You're acting so half-heartedly.

13:24.950 --> 13:28.530
Do you have any aspirations at all?
Of course you don't.

13:29.280 --> 13:33.000
And yet, you possess a silver coin.

13:34.120 --> 13:39.000
I don't need anyone
encroaching on my playing field.

13:39.540 --> 13:42.920
I'll be the last one standing. Nobody else.

13:43.880 --> 13:48.510
Scum like you can spend your lives
rolling across the ground.

13:51.350 --> 13:53.430
Trying to stand is futile.

13:53.430 --> 13:56.480
No human can withstand this gravity.

14:00.310 --> 14:02.400
I can do enough without standing.

14:08.360 --> 14:09.780
<i>The earth split?</i>

14:10.740 --> 14:12.030
<i>Roots?</i>

14:15.660 --> 14:17.960
<i>That's ridiculous.</i>

14:18.370 --> 14:19.540
Huh?

14:20.830 --> 14:24.460
Do you actually like
rolling on the ground, too?

14:31.140 --> 14:32.470
Graviole!

14:39.270 --> 14:42.270
<i>He's faster than earlier!</i>

14:50.530 --> 14:51.740
What's this?

14:57.450 --> 15:03.040
L-L-Lolicon. He's a lolicon.

15:04.210 --> 15:07.630
I-I have to call the police.
He's a criminal.

15:07.630 --> 15:08.760
I'm not.

15:09.050 --> 15:10.800
So, you're aiming to be one?

15:10.800 --> 15:12.970
I said I'm not.

15:13.640 --> 15:15.640
I don't have a Lolita complex.

15:17.310 --> 15:19.190
I have a sister complex.

15:21.150 --> 15:22.520
And that makes it better?

15:22.520 --> 15:23.560
Give it back.

15:23.560 --> 15:25.020
Oh. Okay.

15:27.820 --> 15:29.860
Let me ask you, Mushroom Head.

15:29.860 --> 15:32.820
What's the most precious thing
in this world?

15:33.160 --> 15:35.280
Huh? You're putting me on the spot here.

15:37.290 --> 15:38.830
- Cream pu—
- Wrong.

15:40.540 --> 15:42.330
- Human life.
- Wrong.

15:43.460 --> 15:44.880
- Love.
- Wrong.

15:44.880 --> 15:46.420
- Freedom.
- Wrong.

15:48.010 --> 15:49.340
- Cream pu—
- Wrong!

15:49.510 --> 15:51.130
Wrong, wrong!

15:51.130 --> 15:53.050
Why can't you answer immediately?

15:53.050 --> 15:56.720
One plus one is two.
Yellow and blue makes green.

15:56.720 --> 15:58.600
The answers are obvious.

15:59.140 --> 16:02.100
So, what is the most precious thing
in this world?

16:03.980 --> 16:05.980
My little sister.

16:07.980 --> 16:10.110
Everyone's got different priorities,
don't they?

16:11.110 --> 16:13.320
I am completely disgusted.

16:13.950 --> 16:16.740
This world is full of idiots.

16:17.660 --> 16:18.740
Creepy.

16:25.960 --> 16:28.250
I'm going to drop this bottle off the cliff.

16:28.500 --> 16:31.510
Then, I'll speed up its fall with my magic.

16:31.630 --> 16:32.760
What!?

16:32.970 --> 16:36.800
You'll try to grab the bottle
to save your friends.

16:37.390 --> 16:41.270
And that's when I'll attack you. Sorry.

16:43.640 --> 16:47.440
<i>I can become endlessly demonic
for my little sister's sake.</i>

16:48.360 --> 16:49.610
<i>Endlessly.</i>

16:49.980 --> 16:51.150
Big brother!

16:51.280 --> 16:53.150
You got in another fight, didn't you?

16:53.360 --> 16:54.320
I didn't.

16:54.320 --> 16:55.660
That's definitely a lie!

16:55.740 --> 16:58.410
Here. Sit down so I can heal you.

17:00.080 --> 17:02.450
So why'd you get into a fight?

17:02.450 --> 17:03.960
I tripped and had a nasty fall.

17:03.960 --> 17:05.250
See, a lie!

17:05.250 --> 17:07.330
You're such a bad liar!

17:07.330 --> 17:10.300
I bet you're not even trying!

17:10.300 --> 17:11.090
I am.

17:13.670 --> 17:19.180
I heard you saved a kid
who was being bullied.

17:19.350 --> 17:23.600
That's why they took note of you,
and you come back injured like this, right?

17:25.310 --> 17:26.560
Geez.

17:27.730 --> 17:33.820
But I love how you're clumsy
but kind like that.

17:36.410 --> 17:37.740
I see.

17:38.240 --> 17:42.040
Geez, stop moving! I can't heal you!

17:43.200 --> 17:44.370
Sorry.

17:46.370 --> 17:47.960
Anna. Anna!

17:55.880 --> 17:57.340
Anna.

17:57.840 --> 18:01.720
Apparently it's an incurable disease that
will strip her of her mark and magical power.

18:01.720 --> 18:05.180
The doctor says she has five years at best.

18:05.600 --> 18:06.850
Five years.

18:07.060 --> 18:11.520
If she loses her magic, we'll have to
hand her over to the government.

18:12.320 --> 18:15.030
But if we do that, Anna will...

18:15.240 --> 18:16.990
I'm afraid we'll have no choice.

18:17.490 --> 18:20.740
Oh, why was a child like this
born from our blood.

18:22.030 --> 18:25.750
This is for your sake as well, Lance.

18:26.210 --> 18:31.210
No way. How can I accept
something so cruel?

18:31.540 --> 18:33.920
My little sister didn't do anything!

18:35.300 --> 18:38.880
Don't touch me!
You guys aren't our parents anymore!

18:40.390 --> 18:43.720
Anna. Anna, I'll make sure...

18:44.600 --> 18:48.640
The Bureau of Magic
made this rotten system.

18:49.730 --> 18:55.530
I'll become a Divine Visionary
and make sure to save you!

18:58.900 --> 19:03.490
<i>For your sake, Anna, I'll become...</i>

19:06.200 --> 19:07.410
Graviole!

19:10.830 --> 19:13.420
What will you do, Mushroom Head?

19:20.220 --> 19:22.180
Hamstring Magic.

19:22.340 --> 19:26.930
<i>Hamstring Magic?
I've never heard of any spells like that!</i>

19:27.310 --> 19:28.770
<i>Besides, he's in...</i>

19:30.980 --> 19:32.520
Big Bang Dash.

19:34.020 --> 19:36.440
<i>...starting position?</i>

19:37.280 --> 19:41.030
The choice of losing,
and the choice of not rescuing.

19:41.660 --> 19:43.030
Neither exist for me.

19:55.790 --> 20:00.260
<i>Did he really run down the cliff, catch the bottle,
and come back up in this one instant?</i>

20:00.800 --> 20:04.890
<i>Unbelievable. Is he using
physical enhancement magic?</i>

20:05.300 --> 20:07.520
<i>No, I can't falter now.</i>

20:07.520 --> 20:09.350
<i>I need to help my little sister.</i>

20:09.810 --> 20:11.060
Let's stop this.

20:12.650 --> 20:16.070
You don't seem like a bad guy.

20:16.520 --> 20:19.610
I don't think we should be fighting.

20:21.030 --> 20:24.070
This bottle was empty. It’s fake.

20:34.170 --> 20:35.540
And we're done.

20:36.750 --> 20:37.880
Why?

20:38.090 --> 20:42.220
If you keep going,
you might win silver coins!

20:42.220 --> 20:43.760
Are you screwing with me?

20:43.760 --> 20:46.260
No, not really.

20:46.350 --> 20:47.810
Then why...

20:49.640 --> 20:51.020
I guess...

20:51.020 --> 20:55.520
I'm too clumsy to make
rational decisions about everything.

20:57.650 --> 21:03.780
<i>But I love how you're clumsy
but kind like that.</i>

21:10.620 --> 21:13.500
What a wet blanket.
I'm heading back.

21:13.830 --> 21:16.080
Just like you said,
we'll stop the fight here.

21:19.130 --> 21:22.260
But I did make a bet with you.

21:23.010 --> 21:24.130
Take it.

21:31.890 --> 21:35.600
If we fought for real,
I wonder what would've happened?

21:36.690 --> 21:39.060
Thank you, Mash.

21:39.060 --> 21:40.650
I was so scared!

21:41.070 --> 21:43.490
I had faith in you
that you could pull it off!

21:43.490 --> 21:47.570
Mash, to be modest,
I want you to marry me!

21:47.570 --> 21:48.030
What kind of house would you like?
Of course, the roof will be...

21:48.030 --> 21:50.580
Bamboo it! This is indeed bamboo!
What kind of house would you like?
Of course, the roof will be...

21:53.870 --> 21:56.460
<i>In the end, Lance was a pretty good guy.</i>

21:57.420 --> 22:00.000
<i>And Mash had a thought.</i>

22:00.840 --> 22:04.090
<i>It would’ve been better to open the bottle
after returning to the academy.</i>
